' Listing 4 of Grogono's article (BYTE, July 1979, p. 208): the Towers of
' Hanoi. The peg names are strings passed as parameters and handed on
' through the recursion.
' Transcribed from the scan: the only changes are ^ for the printed up
' arrow, straight quotes, spacing and line breaks outside strings, and these
' comment lines. Strings are as printed (spaces inside strings are read
' from proportional type, so their exact count is approximate).
' The prompt is followed by no new line, so the first move is printed on
' the prompt's line.
"TOWERS OF HANOI!HOW MANY DISKS?" D ? =
D. [ #H,D.,"LEFT","RIGHT","CENTER"; ]

$H %A [ #H,%A 1 -,%B,%D,%C;
        "MOVE " %B " TO " %C "!"
        #H,%A 1 -,%D,%C,%B; ] @
$$
